A hitch log: a frame over 50 ms and three times the frames before it is logged with what it did (shaders compiled and
their time, pipelines made, new textures and their uploads, the draw and sync time, the title thread's recording and
waiting, the files read and their time), to find what stalls a level as it streams. On with XBE_PERF, or always in a
build with asserts (the dev build), whose perf timers it turns on.

diff --git a/runtime/core/diag.h b/runtime/core/diag.h
--- a/runtime/core/diag.h
+++ b/runtime/core/diag.h
@@ -9,6 +9,16 @@
 inline bool Perf() {
